# ---- build concurrency (optional — 0 is the default) ----
# BUILD_SLOTS is the box-wide ceiling on concurrent local builds.
#   0  = UNLIMITED: bin/run-build.sh takes no slot lock, so a build is never held
#        behind another build (the operator, 2026-09-13 — "we never lock and serialize").
#   N  = at most N local builds on this box; the N+1th is told BUILD_DEFERRED and
#        re-offered on the next triage tick. It never waits in line.
# Set a number only where the hardware genuinely needs it (cores/RAM for parallel
# npm builds). Fly-routed projects never reach this gate at all.
#BUILD_SLOTS=0

